lcm_tail_max=5, workers=4
[0] Assumption challenge
  considered vertices:
    runners, gaps, divisor clocks, fixed circle sections, section boundaries,
    wall-crossing events, residues, cover arcs, Fourier/moment modes,
    matroid-like circuits, K33/state-lift obligations, and packet families.
  chosen vertices:
    fixed-margin labelled packet classes and proof sectors.
  preserved LRC predicate:
    strict-counterexample status M(S)<1/14, boundary-vs-open witness status,
    qdiv cover obligations, and named C27/K33/source packet ownership.
  destroyed information:
    raw runner identity and exact wall-crossing order after conversion to labels.
  challenged assumption:
    a counterexample family is not a raw parametric row list; it is a
    fixed-margin packet class plus the non-scalar labels that survive swaps.

[1] arXiv:2606.22636 proof-pattern import
  imported as architecture, not as an LRC theorem.
  fixed-margin binary matrices -> labelled packet incidence matrices
  swap chain within fixed margins -> packet-preserving mutations
  two-row heat-bath comparison -> conditional resampling of two packet rows
  three-row reduction -> local triples of proof-obligation rows
  scalar count sector -> qdiv/q-cover counts
  Johnson harmonic sectors -> boundary-owner, C27/unital, source, K33, gK8 labels

