    qdiv/q-cover count sector > Haar open-vs-boundary sector > source-spectrum pullback > fixed-margin mutation family > C27/unital owner sector > K33 state-lift sector > gK8/L_y moment bridge > unnamed source-kernel bucket > raw residue/tournament shadow

[6] Labelled Packet Theorem target
  For every primitive 13-row S, build its fixed-margin incidence packet:
    rows = q-cover obligations, U14 apex zero/boundary contacts,
           C27 shell states, source-spectrum labels, K33/state-lift flags,
           and boundary-moment/gK8 coordinates when qdiv>14.
  Packet-preserving swaps define families.  A family is safe if each
  count sector or non-scalar sector has a named discharge.
  The only possible strict counterexamples after this theorem would be:
    L1 apex-multiple residual, L2 genuine-wide zero-moment, L3 bounded
    covering core, L4 K33 zero-open state lift, or L5 unnamed source kernel.
  This representative run found no row in the strict or zero-open live buckets.
